<!--meta {"lead": "A toast confirms that something happened, or failed, without taking people away from what they were doing: Request received, Time confirmed, Review not posted.", "description": "Info, success, warning and danger toasts, with action, stacked and persistent forms, in both themes.", "pills": ["<code>role=\"status\"</code> / <code>role=\"alert\"</code> regions", "Status: stable"], "variants": "info, success, warning, danger; with action; stacked; persistent", "states": "entering, default, hover/focus (timer paused), leaving, persistent", "sources": ["notifications/booking-update/info", "notifications/booking-update/success", "notifications/booking-update/danger", "notifications/booking-update/stacked", "notifications/review-feedback/with-action", "notifications/account-feedback/persistent", "notifications/cookie-consent/warning"]} -->
<section class="ds-section" id="overview"><h2><a href="#overview">Overview</a></h2>
  <p>Use a toast for brief feedback about an action the person just took, or an update they are waiting for: "Request received", "Time confirmed", "Details updated". Use an inline <a href="alert.html">alert</a> when the message belongs to one part of the page or must stay (offline, partial data), a <a href="dialog.html">dialog</a> when a decision is required, and the notification centre for anything people need to find later.</p>
  <ul>
    <li><b>Info</b>: news with no judgement ("Request received", "Review ready").</li>
    <li><b>Success</b>: the action worked ("Time confirmed", "Review posted"). Dismisses after 8 seconds.</li>
    <li><b>Warning</b>: something needs a look but nothing failed ("Time needs a change"). Has an action and stays until dismissed or acted on.</li>
    <li><b>Danger</b>: the action failed ("Update could not be sent"). Never auto-dismisses; says the work is safe and offers Retry.</li>
  </ul>
</section>

<section class="ds-section" id="anatomy"><h2><a href="#anatomy">Anatomy</a></h2>
  <div class="ds-anatomy">
    <figure class="ds-anatomy__figure">
      <div class="toast-region toast-region--inline" style="z-index: auto;"><div class="toast toast--warning">{{icon:warning}}<div class="toast__body"><strong class="toast__title">Time needs a change</strong><span class="toast__text">Nia suggested Sun 25 Oct at 11:00 am.</span><button class="toast__action" type="button">View suggestion</button></div><button class="close" type="button" aria-label="Dismiss: Time needs a change">{{icon:close|icon--sm}}</button><span class="toast__progress" aria-hidden="true"></span></div></div>
      <span class="ds-callout" style="left: 18%; top: 16%;" aria-hidden="true">1</span>
      <span class="ds-callout" style="left: 50%; top: 16%;" aria-hidden="true">2</span>
      <span class="ds-callout" style="left: 73%; top: 41%;" aria-hidden="true">3</span>
      <span class="ds-callout" style="left: 49%; top: 57%;" aria-hidden="true">4</span>
      <span class="ds-callout" style="left: 76%; top: 21%;" aria-hidden="true">5</span>
      <span class="ds-callout" style="left: 26%; top: 74%;" aria-hidden="true">6</span>
    </figure>
    <ol class="ds-anatomy__list">
      <li><div><b>Status icon</b><small>20px, the tone's <code>--color-*-icon-inverse</code>; tone is never colour alone.</small></div></li>
      <li><div><b>Title</b><small>Label font; what happened, two to four words.</small></div></li>
      <li><div><b>Text</b><small>Body small; the specific detail (who, when, what next).</small></div></li>
      <li><div><b>Action (optional)</b><small>One underlined text button: Retry, Undo, View appointment.</small></div></li>
      <li><div><b>Dismiss</b><small>24px close button, always present, labelled with the title.</small></div></li>
      <li><div><b>Timer bar (auto-dismiss only)</b><small>2px, 40% of the text colour; pauses on hover and focus.</small></div></li>
    </ol>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="ds-section" id="variants"><h2><a href="#variants">Variants</a></h2>
  <p>Booking updates from the mocks in each tone. Toasts are inverse surfaces (dark on a light page, light on a dark page) so they read above any content.</p>
  {{example:[stack,start]Info, success, warning, danger. Polite tones share one <code>role="status"</code> region; danger goes to the <code>role="alert"</code> region.}}
<div class="toast-region toast-region--inline">
  <div class="toast toast--info">{{icon:info}}<div class="toast__body"><strong class="toast__title">Request received</strong><span class="toast__text">Nia has your request and will reply soon.</span></div><button class="close" type="button" aria-label="Dismiss: Request received">{{icon:close|icon--sm}}</button></div>
  <div class="toast toast--success">{{icon:check-circle}}<div class="toast__body"><strong class="toast__title">Time confirmed</strong><span class="toast__text">Nia confirmed Sat 24 Oct at 10:00 am.</span><button class="toast__action" type="button">View appointment</button></div><button class="close" type="button" aria-label="Dismiss: Time confirmed">{{icon:close|icon--sm}}</button></div>
  <div class="toast toast--warning">{{icon:warning}}<div class="toast__body"><strong class="toast__title">Time needs a change</strong><span class="toast__text">Nia suggested Sun 25 Oct at 11:00 am.</span><button class="toast__action" type="button">View suggestion</button></div><button class="close" type="button" aria-label="Dismiss: Time needs a change">{{icon:close|icon--sm}}</button></div>
  <div class="toast toast--danger">{{icon:alert-circle}}<div class="toast__body"><strong class="toast__title">Update could not be sent</strong><span class="toast__text">Your request is still saved. Retry when connected.</span><button class="toast__action" type="button">Retry</button></div><button class="close" type="button" aria-label="Dismiss: Update could not be sent">{{icon:close|icon--sm}}</button></div>
</div>
  {{/example}}
  <h3>With an undo action</h3>
  {{example:[stack,start]Offer Undo only when the action can really be reversed, here a phone number that was just changed. A posted review has nothing to undo.}}
<div class="toast-region toast-region--inline">
  <div class="toast toast--success">{{icon:check-circle}}<div class="toast__body"><strong class="toast__title">Details updated</strong><span class="toast__text">Nia can reach you at your new number.</span><button class="toast__action" type="button">Undo</button></div><button class="close" type="button" aria-label="Dismiss: Details updated">{{icon:close|icon--sm}}</button><span class="toast__progress" aria-hidden="true"></span></div>
</div>
  {{/example}}
  <h3>Stacked</h3>
  {{example:[stack,start]Newest at the bottom, nearest the edge. At most three; older ones live on in the notification centre.}}
<div class="toast-region toast-region--inline">
  <div class="toast toast--info">{{icon:info}}<div class="toast__body"><strong class="toast__title">Details saved locally</strong><span class="toast__text">We’ll sync your changes when connected.</span></div><button class="close" type="button" aria-label="Dismiss: Details saved locally">{{icon:close|icon--sm}}</button></div>
  <div class="toast toast--success">{{icon:check-circle}}<div class="toast__body"><strong class="toast__title">Details updated</strong><span class="toast__text">Nia can reach you at your new number.</span></div><button class="close" type="button" aria-label="Dismiss: Details updated">{{icon:close|icon--sm}}</button></div>
  <div class="toast toast--danger">{{icon:alert-circle}}<div class="toast__body"><strong class="toast__title">Changes not saved</strong><span class="toast__text">Your edits are still here. Please try again.</span><button class="toast__action" type="button">Retry</button></div><button class="close" type="button" aria-label="Dismiss: Changes not saved">{{icon:close|icon--sm}}</button></div>
</div>
  {{/example}}
</section>

<section class="ds-section" id="sizes" data-na="Toasts have one size: 24rem wide from 640px, full width minus 16px margins below it."><h2><a href="#sizes">Sizes</a></h2></section>

<section class="ds-section" id="states"><h2><a href="#states">States</a></h2>
  <p>A toast slides up on entry (<code>--duration-base</code>, enter easing), waits, and fades down on exit. Hover and focus inside it pause the timer. The action and dismiss buttons have the usual button states; focus is forced here with <code>data-state</code>.</p>
  <div class="ds-matrix"><table>
    <thead><tr><th scope="col">Tone</th><th scope="col">Default</th><th scope="col">Action focused (paused)</th><th scope="col">Dismiss focused</th><th scope="col">Leaving</th><th scope="col">Persistent</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><th scope="row">Info</th><td><div class="toast toast--info">{{icon:info}}<div class="toast__body"><strong class="toast__title">Review ready</strong><span class="toast__text">Share how your visit went.</span></div><button class="close" type="button" aria-label="Dismiss: Review ready">{{icon:close|icon--sm}}</button><span class="toast__progress" aria-hidden="true"></span></div></td><td><div class="toast toast--info">{{icon:info}}<div class="toast__body"><strong class="toast__title">Review ready</strong><span class="toast__text">Share how your visit went.</span><button class="toast__action" type="button" data-state="focus">Write review</button></div><button class="close" type="button" aria-label="Dismiss: Review ready (paused)">{{icon:close|icon--sm}}</button></div></td><td><div class="toast toast--info">{{icon:info}}<div class="toast__body"><strong class="toast__title">Review ready</strong><span class="toast__text">Share how your visit went.</span></div><button class="close" type="button" aria-label="Dismiss: Review ready (focused)" data-state="focus">{{icon:close|icon--sm}}</button></div></td><td><div class="toast toast--info" style="opacity: 0.5; translate: 0 var(--space-1);">{{icon:info}}<div class="toast__body"><strong class="toast__title">Review ready</strong><span class="toast__text">Share how your visit went.</span></div><button class="close" type="button" aria-label="Dismiss: Review ready (leaving)">{{icon:close|icon--sm}}</button></div></td><td><div class="toast toast--info">{{icon:info}}<div class="toast__body"><strong class="toast__title">Your privacy choices</strong><span class="toast__text">Choose whether optional usage data may be stored.</span><button class="toast__action" type="button">Choose</button></div><button class="close" type="button" aria-label="Dismiss: Your privacy choices">{{icon:close|icon--sm}}</button></div></td></tr>
      <tr><th scope="row">Success</th><td><div class="toast toast--success">{{icon:check-circle}}<div class="toast__body"><strong class="toast__title">Preferences saved</strong><span class="toast__text">You can change them any time.</span></div><button class="close" type="button" aria-label="Dismiss: Preferences saved">{{icon:close|icon--sm}}</button><span class="toast__progress" aria-hidden="true"></span></div></td><td><div class="toast toast--success">{{icon:check-circle}}<div class="toast__body"><strong class="toast__title">Details updated</strong><span class="toast__text">Nia can reach you at your new number.</span><button class="toast__action" type="button" data-state="focus">Undo</button></div><button class="close" type="button" aria-label="Dismiss: Details updated (paused)">{{icon:close|icon--sm}}</button></div></td><td><div class="toast toast--success">{{icon:check-circle}}<div class="toast__body"><strong class="toast__title">Preferences saved</strong><span class="toast__text">You can change them any time.</span></div><button class="close" type="button" aria-label="Dismiss: Preferences saved (focused)" data-state="focus">{{icon:close|icon--sm}}</button></div></td><td><div class="toast toast--success" style="opacity: 0.5; translate: 0 var(--space-1);">{{icon:check-circle}}<div class="toast__body"><strong class="toast__title">Preferences saved</strong><span class="toast__text">You can change them any time.</span></div><button class="close" type="button" aria-label="Dismiss: Preferences saved (leaving)">{{icon:close|icon--sm}}</button></div></td><td>Not used: success always times out.</td></tr>
      <tr><th scope="row">Warning</th><td><div class="toast toast--warning">{{icon:warning}}<div class="toast__body"><strong class="toast__title">Verify your email</strong><span class="toast__text">Open the link sent to maya.chen@example.com.</span><button class="toast__action" type="button">Resend email</button></div><button class="close" type="button" aria-label="Dismiss: Verify your email">{{icon:close|icon--sm}}</button></div></td><td><div class="toast toast--warning">{{icon:warning}}<div class="toast__body"><strong class="toast__title">Verify your email</strong><span class="toast__text">Open the link sent to maya.chen@example.com.</span><button class="toast__action" type="button" data-state="focus">Resend email</button></div><button class="close" type="button" aria-label="Dismiss: Verify your email (paused)">{{icon:close|icon--sm}}</button></div></td><td><div class="toast toast--warning">{{icon:warning}}<div class="toast__body"><strong class="toast__title">Verify your email</strong><span class="toast__text">Open the link sent to maya.chen@example.com.</span></div><button class="close" type="button" aria-label="Dismiss: Verify your email (focused)" data-state="focus">{{icon:close|icon--sm}}</button></div></td><td><div class="toast toast--warning" style="opacity: 0.5; translate: 0 var(--space-1);">{{icon:warning}}<div class="toast__body"><strong class="toast__title">Verify your email</strong><span class="toast__text">Open the link sent to maya.chen@example.com.</span></div><button class="close" type="button" aria-label="Dismiss: Verify your email (leaving)">{{icon:close|icon--sm}}</button></div></td><td><div class="toast toast--warning">{{icon:warning}}<div class="toast__body"><strong class="toast__title">Choice needed</strong><span class="toast__text">Select a preference to continue.</span><button class="toast__action" type="button">Choose</button></div><button class="close" type="button" aria-label="Dismiss: Choice needed">{{icon:close|icon--sm}}</button></div></td></tr>
      <tr><th scope="row">Danger</th><td><div class="toast toast--danger">{{icon:alert-circle}}<div class="toast__body"><strong class="toast__title">Review not posted</strong><span class="toast__text">Your words are saved. Please try again.</span><button class="toast__action" type="button">Retry</button></div><button class="close" type="button" aria-label="Dismiss: Review not posted">{{icon:close|icon--sm}}</button></div></td><td><div class="toast toast--danger">{{icon:alert-circle}}<div class="toast__body"><strong class="toast__title">Review not posted</strong><span class="toast__text">Your words are saved. Please try again.</span><button class="toast__action" type="button" data-state="focus">Retry</button></div><button class="close" type="button" aria-label="Dismiss: Review not posted (paused)">{{icon:close|icon--sm}}</button></div></td><td><div class="toast toast--danger">{{icon:alert-circle}}<div class="toast__body"><strong class="toast__title">Review not posted</strong><span class="toast__text">Your words are saved. Please try again.</span></div><button class="close" type="button" aria-label="Dismiss: Review not posted (focused)" data-state="focus">{{icon:close|icon--sm}}</button></div></td><td><div class="toast toast--danger" style="opacity: 0.5; translate: 0 var(--space-1);">{{icon:alert-circle}}<div class="toast__body"><strong class="toast__title">Review not posted</strong><span class="toast__text">Leaves only when dismissed.</span></div><button class="close" type="button" aria-label="Dismiss: Review not posted (leaving)">{{icon:close|icon--sm}}</button></div></td><td>Always persistent (shown in Default).</td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table></div>
  <p>The Leaving column shows a mid-exit frame; in product, <code>data-state="leaving"</code> plays the <code>fade-out</code> animation over <code>--duration-base</code> and the element is removed when it ends.</p>
  <h3>Both themes</h3>
  {{themes:stack}}<div class="toast-region toast-region--inline"><div class="toast toast--success">{{icon:check-circle}}<div class="toast__body"><strong class="toast__title">Time confirmed</strong><span class="toast__text">Nia confirmed Sat 24 Oct at 10:00 am.</span></div><button class="close" type="button" aria-label="Dismiss: Time confirmed">{{icon:close|icon--sm}}</button></div><div class="toast toast--danger">{{icon:alert-circle}}<div class="toast__body"><strong class="toast__title">Update could not be sent</strong><span class="toast__text">Your request is still saved.</span><button class="toast__action" type="button">Retry</button></div><button class="close" type="button" aria-label="Dismiss: Update could not be sent">{{icon:close|icon--sm}}</button></div></div>{{/themes}}
  <ul>
    <li><b>Auto-dismiss</b>: info and success toasts without an action leave after 8 seconds (WCAG 2.2.1), pausing while hovered or focused. Toasts with an action stay at least 10 seconds.</li>
    <li><b>Persistent</b>: warning and danger toasts, and anything that asks for a choice (cookie consent), stay until dismissed or acted on. They show no timer bar.</li>
  </ul>
</section>

<section class="ds-section" id="responsive"><h2><a href="#responsive">Responsive behaviour</a></h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Below <code>--layout-breakpoint-sm</code> (640px) the region spans the bottom of the screen with 16px margins and respects <code>env(safe-area-inset-bottom)</code>.</li>
    <li>From 640px the region docks bottom right, 24rem wide, 24px from the edges.</li>
    <li><code>.toast-region--top</code> is the assertive region for danger toasts: it sits at the top (16px from the edge) so it never overlaps the polite region at the bottom.</li>
    <li>A region is never taller than the viewport minus 32px; it scrolls (<code>overflow-y: auto</code>) and toast text and actions wrap and break long words, so with 200% text every control stays reachable.</li>
    <li>Toasts never cover the focused element or a primary action (WCAG 2.4.11).</li>
  </ul>
</section>

<section class="ds-section" id="theming"><h2><a href="#theming">Theming</a></h2>
  <p>Component tokens <code>--toast-bg</code> (<code>--color-bg-inverse</code>), <code>--toast-fg</code> (<code>--color-fg-inverse</code>) and <code>--toast-icon</code> (the tone's <code>--color-*-icon-inverse</code>). In light mode the toast is grey-900 with 300-step icons; in dark mode it flips to grey-100 with 600/700-step icons, so it still stands out from a dark page.</p>
  <pre><code>/* A raised (non-inverse) toast for a calm surface */
.toast--raised { --toast-bg: var(--color-bg-surface-raised); --toast-fg: var(--color-fg-default); }</code></pre>
</section>

<section class="ds-section" id="accessibility"><h2><a href="#accessibility">Accessibility</a></h2>
  <h3>Role and pattern</h3>
  <p>Two live regions exist on every page from load: <code>&lt;div class="toast-region" role="status" aria-live="polite"&gt;</code> for info, success and warning, and a second region with <code>role="alert"</code> for danger. Toasts are inserted into the right region; a toast never carries its own live role inside another live region (<a href="https://www.w3.org/WAI/ARIA/apg/patterns/alert/">APG Alert</a>).</p>
  <h3>Keyboard</h3>
  <table class="ds-table ds-keys"><thead><tr><th scope="col">Key</th><th scope="col">Action</th></tr></thead><tbody>
    <tr><td><kbd>Tab</kbd> / <kbd>Shift</kbd>+<kbd>Tab</kbd></td><td>Reaches the action and dismiss buttons in DOM order; focus inside pauses the timer.</td></tr>
    <tr><td><kbd>Enter</kbd> / <kbd>Space</kbd></td><td>Activates the action or dismisses.</td></tr>
    <tr><td><kbd>Esc</kbd></td><td>Dismisses the focused toast and returns focus to where it was before.</td></tr>
  </tbody></table>
  <h3>Focus</h3>
  <p>Toasts never take focus when they appear. After a dismiss, focus returns to the element that was focused before the person tabbed into the toast, or to the next toast. The focus ring inside a toast keeps the shared width and offset but uses the toast's text colour (<code>--toast-fg</code>): the shared <code>--color-focus-ring</code> is under 3:1 on the inverse surface. This is the one exception to "one ring everywhere".</p>
  <h3>Labelling</h3>
  <p>The title and text are announced together. The dismiss button names the toast ("Dismiss: Time confirmed"); the action names its result ("View appointment", "Retry"), not "View update".</p>
  <h3>Contrast</h3>
  <div class="ds-example__canvas ds-example__canvas--stack" style="padding: 0; gap: var(--space-2);">
    {{pair:Text on toast|--color-fg-inverse|--color-bg-inverse|4.5}}
    {{pair:Info icon|--color-info-icon-inverse|--color-bg-inverse|3}}
    {{pair:Success icon|--color-success-icon-inverse|--color-bg-inverse|3}}
    {{pair:Warning icon|--color-warning-icon-inverse|--color-bg-inverse|3}}
    {{pair:Danger icon|--color-danger-icon-inverse|--color-bg-inverse|3}}
    {{pair:Focus ring in a toast|--color-fg-inverse|--color-bg-inverse|3}}
  </div>
  <h3>Motion</h3>
  <p>Slide-up entry and fade-down exit over <code>--duration-base</code>; reduced motion zeroes both, so toasts appear and disappear in place.</p>
  <h3>Touch</h3>
  <p>The dismiss and action buttons are 24px targets with at least 12px between them. Swipe to dismiss is an enhancement; the close button is always there.</p>
</section>

<section class="ds-section" id="content"><h2><a href="#content">Content</a></h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Title: what happened, two to four words: "Time confirmed", "Review posted", "Changes not saved".</li>
    <li>Text: the specific detail in one sentence: who, when, what next. "Nia confirmed Sat 24 Oct at 10:00 am."</li>
    <li>Failures say the work is safe and what to do: "Your words are saved. Please try again." plus Retry.</li>
    <li>One action at most; name its result. Offer Undo only when the action can be undone.</li>
    <li>No "Success!" or "Error!" titles; the icon and tone already say that.</li>
  </ul>
</section>

<section class="ds-section" id="do-dont"><h2><a href="#do-dont">Do and don't</a></h2>
  <div class="ds-dodont">
    <figure class="ds-do"><div class="ds-example__canvas"><div class="toast-region toast-region--inline"><div class="toast toast--danger">{{icon:alert-circle}}<div class="toast__body"><strong class="toast__title">Update could not be sent</strong><span class="toast__text">Your request is still saved.</span><button class="toast__action" type="button">Retry</button></div><button class="close" type="button" aria-label="Dismiss: Update could not be sent (do)">{{icon:close|icon--sm}}</button></div></div></div><figcaption>An icon and title give the tone without colour; Retry is offered and the toast stays.</figcaption></figure>
    <figure class="ds-dont"><div class="ds-example__canvas"><div class="toast-region toast-region--inline"><div class="toast toast--danger"><div class="toast__body"><strong class="toast__title">Update could not be sent</strong><span class="toast__text">Your request is still saved.</span></div><button class="close" type="button" aria-label="Dismiss notification">×</button></div></div></div><figcaption>No icon, so the tone is invisible on the dark toast; a "×" glyph and a generic "Dismiss notification" label, as in the first mocks.</figcaption></figure>
    <figure class="ds-do"><div class="ds-example__canvas"><div class="toast-region toast-region--inline"><div class="toast toast--success">{{icon:check-circle}}<div class="toast__body"><strong class="toast__title">Time confirmed</strong><span class="toast__text">Nia confirmed Sat 24 Oct at 10:00 am.</span><button class="toast__action" type="button">View appointment</button></div><button class="close" type="button" aria-label="Dismiss: Time confirmed (do)">{{icon:close|icon--sm}}</button></div></div></div><figcaption>The action leads somewhere useful.</figcaption></figure>
    <figure class="ds-dont"><div class="ds-example__canvas"><div class="toast-region toast-region--inline"><div class="toast toast--success">{{icon:check-circle}}<div class="toast__body"><strong class="toast__title">Time confirmed</strong><span class="toast__text">Nia confirmed Sat 24 Oct at 10:00 am.</span><button class="toast__action" type="button">Undo</button></div><button class="close" type="button" aria-label="Dismiss: Time confirmed (don't)">{{icon:close|icon--sm}}</button></div></div></div><figcaption>"Undo" on something the customer cannot undo (Nia confirmed the time), as on the first booking-update success mock.</figcaption></figure>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="ds-section" id="tokens"><h2><a href="#tokens">Tokens</a></h2>
  <div class="ds-table-wrap"><table class="ds-table">
    <thead><tr><th scope="col">Part</th><th scope="col">Token</th><th scope="col">Light</th><th scope="col">Dark</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      {{tok:Background|--color-bg-inverse}}
      {{tok:Text|--color-fg-inverse}}
      {{tok:Info / success icon|--color-info-icon-inverse|--color-success-icon-inverse}}
      {{tok:Warning / danger icon|--color-warning-icon-inverse|--color-danger-icon-inverse}}
      {{tok:Title / text font|--text-label|--text-body-sm}}
      {{tok:Padding / gap|--space-4|--space-3}}
      {{tok:Shape|--radius-md}}
      {{tok:Elevation|--shadow-3}}
      {{tok:Layer|--z-toast}}
      {{tok:Enter / exit|--duration-base|--ease-enter|--ease-exit}}
      {{tok:Dismiss target|--target-min}}
    </tbody>
  </table></div>
  <p>Component tokens: <code>--toast-bg</code>, <code>--toast-fg</code>, <code>--toast-icon</code>.</p>
</section>

<section class="ds-section" id="code"><h2><a href="#code">Code</a></h2>
  <pre><code>&lt;div class="toast-region" role="status" aria-live="polite"&gt;
  &lt;div class="toast toast--success"&gt;
    &lt;svg class="icon" aria-hidden="true" viewBox="0 0 24 24"&gt;…&lt;/svg&gt;
    &lt;div class="toast__body"&gt;
      &lt;strong class="toast__title"&gt;Time confirmed&lt;/strong&gt;
      &lt;span class="toast__text"&gt;Nia confirmed Sat 24 Oct at 10:00 am.&lt;/span&gt;
      &lt;button class="toast__action" type="button"&gt;View appointment&lt;/button&gt;
    &lt;/div&gt;
    &lt;button class="close" type="button" aria-label="Dismiss: Time confirmed"&gt;…&lt;/button&gt;
  &lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class="toast-region toast-region--top" role="alert" aria-live="assertive"&gt;&lt;!-- danger toasts --&gt;&lt;/div&gt;</code></pre>
  <table class="ds-table"><thead><tr><th scope="col">Class / attribute</th><th scope="col">Effect</th></tr></thead><tbody>
    <tr><td><code>.toast-region</code></td><td>Fixed region at the bottom (full width on phones, 24rem bottom right from 640px).</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>.toast-region--top</code> / <code>.toast-region--inline</code></td><td>Top placement for the assertive (danger) region / static placement for documentation.</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>.toast</code> + <code>.toast--info|success|warning|danger</code></td><td>Inverse toast with the tone's icon colour.</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>.toast__body</code> <code>.toast__title</code> <code>.toast__text</code> <code>.toast__action</code></td><td>Content parts.</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>.toast .close</code></td><td>Dismiss button; needs <code>aria-label</code>.</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>.toast__progress</code></td><td>Timer bar for auto-dismissing toasts.</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>data-state="leaving"</code></td><td>Plays the exit animation.</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>role="status"</code> / <code>role="alert"</code></td><td>On the two regions, never on a toast inside them.</td></tr>
  </tbody></table>
</section>

<section class="ds-section" id="sources"><h2><a href="#sources">Sources</a></h2>
  <p>Extracted from these mocks:</p>
  <ul>
    {{mock:notifications/booking-update/info|Request received}}
    {{mock:notifications/booking-update/success|Time confirmed, with View appointment}}
    {{mock:notifications/booking-update/danger|Update could not be sent}}
    {{mock:notifications/booking-update/stacked|three tones stacked}}
    {{mock:notifications/review-feedback/with-action|action button}}
    {{mock:notifications/account-feedback/persistent|persistent info}}
    {{mock:notifications/cookie-consent/warning|Choice needed}}
  </ul>
  <p>Drift fixed during extraction: toasts had no status icon, so the tone was colour only on the dark toast (system adds the tone icon and keeps a title); the <code>role="status"</code> region wrapped a danger toast with its own <code>role="alert"</code> (nested live regions; system uses separate polite and assertive regions); success toasts offered "Undo" for actions the customer cannot undo, such as Nia confirming a time; with-action toasts used the generic "View update"; the close button was a "×" glyph labelled "Dismiss notification" (system: close icon labelled with the toast title); toast text was dimmed to 90% opacity (removed; contrast comes from tokens).</p>
</section>
